WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.020
So, I'm also really excited as well.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.280
(Sam) Now basically...so basically...

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.660
So, basically...

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.320
(Dwayne Johnson) Alright, let's try; and so, this happens to people all the time

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.040
(Wren) Twenty seven visual effects shots in this piece.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.060
Well...

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.920
(Carmichael) Today's Tuesday.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.460
(Wren) Yeah...

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.860
(Carmichael) This should be done by Friday.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.560
You have three days to do 27 shots.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.360
(Wren) No, this isn't, this isn't going to be done by Friday

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.900
(Sam) I'm in New York City today, because I'm shooting a promotional

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.320
video with Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.840
This is a really intense experience for myself, because he is literally

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.180
the biggest celebrity right now.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.860
And I have to admit, I'm usually not starstruck, but I'm...

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.780
I'm pretty nervous about meeting him because he's such an intense guy.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:06.000
I have been selected to go and shoot our promotional video for Lifeline with him.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.060
We only have twenty minutes with him

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.980
We have all night to prepare and set up our set for the shoot.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.580
We're going to see how all of this goes.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.000
Wish me luck.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.080
About two in the morning now.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.840
We have taken our large hotel suite here,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.380
and we converted it into a small set.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:30.660
Complete with lights and a white backdrop

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.860
because tomorrow morning we have twenty minutes to shoot and we have to be 100% ready.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.920
So, we just spent all night pre-lighting everything.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.820
This hotel room is so fancy and crazy.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.460
There's even, like, a secret door here.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:50.060
That opens up to a whole other room.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.180
Easily the most expensive looking room I've ever stayed in in my entire life.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.980
(Wren) That means I have to average nine shots per day.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.800
Excluding whatever shots I'm able to get done today.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.380
Most of the effects are...

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.500
compositing a green screen element onto a wall,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.100
and that's actually pretty simple, because

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.140
it's a shadow. You're just going to turn that plate into

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.260
black and white.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:34.760
I'm able to- I'm able to kick through these shadow effects pretty quickly.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.140
We have to have all the effects done by tomorrow, and

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.020
there's still a lot of effects left to do.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:40.780
So Gabe...

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.840
I am- I am recruiting you to do some very tedious stuff.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.580
It takes a lot of time.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.760
Because if you can take that off my plate, I think I might be able to finish all the rest of the effects.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.820
That's why I'm screen capturing, Carmichael...

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.760
(Carmichael) You're screen-capturing this shot, this monitor.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.260
(Wren) Yeah.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.080
(Carmichael) But you're describing what's happening on this monitor.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.340
(Wren) But...

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.240
So, Brett's getting dragged across the floor,

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.060
and we have to basically paint out all of

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:10.700
Jake, but not of the backpack.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.280
(Gabe) Yeah.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.780
(Wren) So we got the footage here,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.660
I turn it off; we have an exact replica of the background.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.000
Do a pass where you literally put a mask

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.380
straight up through and over.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.400
Set that to subtract...

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:28.920
Now that we basically cut out Jake for the entirety of the shot, we need

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.680
we need to add back in Brett.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.380
So that's how this is a two stage process here.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.320
(Sam) It's a fact that we're out of water.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.900
It's 12:47, and we are minutes away from actually shooting this thing,

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.120
And I'm here with all sorts of people.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:50.860
We're with Dennis, our DP, Scott, from Seven7Box, with Kurt, who's generally just a cool guy

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.920
and helped us figure out this entire lighting setup.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.820
and [unintelligible], but he's not here right now.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.420
Everyone's finally starting to arrive, meaning

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.480
it's about to get very, very real.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.580
(greetings around)

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.580
(Dwayne Johnson) I see, okay, so, I see, so

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.180
[unintelligible] copy all the way through,

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:38.320
two times, just to get an idea of what we're doing.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.280
(Sam) Exactly

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.320
(Dwayne Johnson) Yeah, so what really just happens

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.120
to be in that space, in terms of promotion.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.400
(Sam) Also, like contemplative, like

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.600
like you don't know, you don't quite know how this works.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.380
They don't know that time travel is involved at all.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.600
So to them, it's just a fluke.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.780
(Wren) Gabe's actually pretty good at After Effects, so

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.160
I've got no worries.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.160
Should I be worried?

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.300
This video has 29 visual effects shots.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.560
The vast majority of them aren't too complicated, and I

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.860
can go through fairly quickly.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.000
I've already kicked out, I think, 6 shots today.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.500
Rotoscoping is just one of those things that takes a lot of time.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.740
But the time that it would take for me to do the backpack shot, just roto-ing out the backpack

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:30.840
and getting that shot done, I could have done 2 or 3 shadow shots.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:36.680
So just logistically speaking, with our schedule, it makes more sense to pass that off to someone else.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.080
(Gabe) Wren makes it look so easy...

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.740
(Wren) Gabe's really good at animation and whatnot, After Effects...

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.540
Considering this is the first time he's used the roto brush,

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.200
It's hard for me to say how long it'll take him to do

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.180
It'd probably take me...

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:59.020
I'm not even remotely worried that Gabe isn't going to get this done.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:02.020
We're wasting time here. I could be doing some green-screening,

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.340
(Carmichael) That's not my time that's being wasted!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.660
(Wren) It's my time! That's my point!

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.360
(Carmichael) Yeah, who's responsible for that?

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.400
(Wren) That...but...you brought me in here.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.820
Gabe finished those two shots. They're excellent.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:18.740
Good job Gabe.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.180
(Carmichael) Is he going to do more?

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:20.900
(Wren) No.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.940
(Carmichael) If he did those so quickly,

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.760
like, give him more work!

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.860
(Wren) Not the end just yet, got another couple hours.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.680
I have, since we last talked,

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.280
finishing up this one right now, so that's three more.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.760
I'm almost done with this shot, so...

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.840
I actually think I might be able to get all of these done by tomorrow.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.240
Wait, so, this is

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.820
Thursday evening, right now.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.260
And this is going up in tomorrow's vlog?

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:00.960
(Carmichael) Yeah!

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.060
(Wren) Hey, look at you guys!

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:07.460
So we have shots we have to film, and there's a drone shot I need to get.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:11.420
(Carmichael) And you're going to do all of that tomorrow.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:14.400
Yeah, and there's like a whole bunch of work here.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.500
Ooh, Gabe can help me with that stuff.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.460
(Gabe) What stuff?

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.520
(Wren) I'll tell you tomorrow.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.260
(Gabe) I'm not going to be here tomorrow.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:26.860
Who is this master?

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.840
Jonathon...DeBoz...

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.480
This kid is a comedic genius.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.420
Gold. It's gold!

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:44.120
Go watch that video. Johnyboz is great.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.160
I've pretty much stop stuck with it ever since

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:46.720
you know

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.680
working-out every day

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.080
the only down side is that

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.140
I can't wear shirts with sleeves anymore my muscles are to big

